<title>DENMARK: Danish April unemployment falls to 7.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish April unemployment falls to 7.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's seasonally adjusted unemployment was 7.9 percent of the workforce in April 1997, down from 8.0 percent in March, the National Statistics Office said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>				 April 1997    March 1997   April 1996</p>
<p>    Unemployment rate    7.9 pct	     8.0 pct   *9.0 pct</p>
<p>     Total unemployed    221,300	    *222,700   *251,200</p>
<p>*Revised All above figures seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>NOTE - A panel of economists polled by Reuters had on average forecast seasonally adjusted April year-on-year unemployment of 7.9 percent. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652.</p>
</text>
